trajectory.patch:
The Kconfig warning indicates that `CONFIG_STDOUT_CONSOLE` could not be enabled due to an unsatisfied dependency, which is a known issue in some Zephyr versions when using sysbuild. This means that `printf` calls will not be directed to the console.

The fix involves two parts:
1.  Remove the problematic `CONFIG_STDOUT_CONSOLE=y` from the project configuration to resolve the Kconfig warning.
2.  Replace the `printf` calls in the source code with `printk`. Since the test enables `CONFIG_ZTEST`, which in turn selects `CONFIG_PRINTK`, `printk` is available and will correctly output messages to the console.

This approach resolves the configuration error while preserving the intended logging functionality of the test.

